// x14 "Four Stars" (script v3, 2026-10-26, docs/x14-four-stars.md). Ross: "Let's do the first one, just crank the categorical tone up to the max": the statement "A 4-star review is a 1-star review with manners."
// Chuck gives Ross's coffee four stars; Ross tries a free latte, a marriage proposal and a dive over the counter to get the fifth, gets it, and Chuck changes it to three: "Owner tackled me."
// Ross is jack-tyler (as in x08-x13), Chuck jack-chris-boston (as in x10-x13).
// Format: see scripts/voice-gen.mjs (lines, directions) and scripts/voice-build.py (cast, plan, gaps, lead, tableSfx). Take k of a line uses direction k.
{
 "title": "Four Stars",
 "cast": {"ross": 1, "chuck": 1},
 "runnerUp": {},
 "lines": [
// right after he slams the phone on the counter, purple, at the top of his voice
  {"n": 1, "char": "ross", "text": "FOUR STARS?!", "dirs": [
   {"t": "[outraged] [shouting]", "st": 0.25, "sy": 0.8},
   {"t": "[appalled] [yelling]", "st": 0.25, "sy": 0.8},
   {"t": "[furious] [loud]", "st": 0.3, "sy": 0.75}
  ]},
// beaming, two thumbs up: he means it as a compliment
  {"n": 2, "char": "chuck", "text": "Four stars is GOOD!", "dirs": [
   {"t": "[cheerful] [proud]", "st": 0.4, "sy": 0.55},
   {"t": "[happy] [enthusiastic]", "st": 0.4, "sy": 0.55},
   {"t": "[friendly] [upbeat]", "st": 0.45, "sy": 0.5}
  ]},
// leaning over the counter, stabbing a finger at him: the statement, no doubt in it
